{"type":"standard","title":"Pete Sessions","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pete Sessions</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q437852","titles":{"canonical":"Pete_Sessions","normalized":"Pete Sessions","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Pete Sessions</span></span>"},"pageid":966515,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Pete_Sessions_Congressional_ID_photo_117.jpg/330px-Pete_Sessions_Congressional_ID_photo_117.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":404},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Pete_Sessions_Congressional_ID_photo_117.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":335,"height":410},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1378193042","tid":"7cde56d3-bf20-11f1-b86e-757453c301c8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T11:49:28Z","description":"American politician (born 1955)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Sessions","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Sessions?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Sessions?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pete_Sessions"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Sessions","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Pete_Sessions","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Sessions?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Pete_Sessions"}},"extract":"Peter Anderson Sessions is an American politician who serves in the United States House of Representatives for Texas's 17th congressional district as a member of the Republican Party. He chaired the House Rules Committee from 2013 to 2019 and is a former chair of the National Republican Congressional Committee.","extract_html":"<p><b>Peter Anderson Sessions</b> is an American politician who serves in the United States House of Representatives for Texas's 17th congressional district as a member of the Republican Party. He chaired the House Rules Committee from 2013 to 2019 and is a former chair of the National Republican Congressional Committee.</p>"}